[{:db/id "q-65571/selection/751c07c835941eaca31781573c15b06b9426f5f2f4241ac45abc1c25f7716c0d" :answer/id #uuid "feb40eb3-62fe-52dd-8a15-caddede53097" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65571/selection/1799e19c9a3a0d0b1889be2c54ab73f5730109da85155b3b8b0ccf6c4adbeaca" :answer/id #uuid "4a8a48ad-7fbc-5d7d-b628-66506c916a76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65571/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" :answer/id #uuid "44f1d945-325e-5235-a7da-c40e8995a9bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65571/selection/df0a02eee36ca5d9f8ef916941b9f30bd0840177cc79b5ea94ec34b1671c0f53" :answer/id #uuid "aa6368ee-90e3-5cb1-8d37-197ba61c328c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65571/selection/d62732e72e17b0393290bd9e548ef368f6b7424bded817d038b07db5bf5fcb98" :answer/id #uuid "05ba1499-ac25-5d08-b8ba-ed30e10d71fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65571/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdf59e94-c44c-520b-a6ea-c9da07142fd6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-65571/selection/751c07c835941eaca31781573c15b06b9426f5f2f4241ac45abc1c25f7716c0d" :answer-field/choices ["q-65571/selection/751c07c835941eaca31781573c15b06b9426f5f2f4241ac45abc1c25f7716c0d" "q-65571/selection/1799e19c9a3a0d0b1889be2c54ab73f5730109da85155b3b8b0ccf6c4adbeaca" "q-65571/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" "q-65571/selection/df0a02eee36ca5d9f8ef916941b9f30bd0840177cc79b5ea94ec34b1671c0f53" "q-65571/selection/d62732e72e17b0393290bd9e548ef368f6b7424bded817d038b07db5bf5fcb98"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65571" :question/id #uuid "ad1e1c5f-8601-5df4-a3fc-7ce84f2d264b" :question/math-academy-id "q-65571" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069862/assets/2f11d5b11c53f7b826291e0b7e95828f57d6f1242b768baf12c874be229b2935.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3x}{5}+C),$ where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of $C?$" :question/worked-solution "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3x}{5}+C) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3}{5}(x+\\frac{5C}{3}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $x+\\frac{5C}{3}$ indicates that the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3}{5}(x+\\frac{5C}{3}))$ is a horizontal translation of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3x}{5}).$ Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069862/assets/5e9b6568ec493d95db6fe72a6a19024326c5b920629e9ff44a85db54089aa2a6.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3x}{5})$ by $\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ units to the right. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5C}{3}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,⟹\\,C=(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})(\\frac{3}{5})\\,⟹\\,C=-\\frac{\\pi }{5}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ is in this interval, the value of $C$ is $-\\frac{\\pi }{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-65571/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84355770-5926-5be6-9b9f-c13bb05599ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65571"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-79194"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069862/assets/a41a721eab2eb97e8b7b30ddf877e37a48d2b74eeef82ab0a4b72f3bb4a93603.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+C),$ where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of $C?$" :question/worked-solution "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+C) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2(x+\\frac{C}{2}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $x+\\frac{C}{2}$ indicates that the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2(x+\\frac{C}{2}))$ is a horizontal translation of $y=tan\\,(2x).$ Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069862/assets/f08846ce1f79cd14c593fbf37360fb8169a26704c956506ca0deedb8025e3b39.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)$ by $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ units to the right. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\frac{C}{2}=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\,⟹\\,C=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-142000/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "e58864ec-5f87-5414-bdde-7a3d7aca3efb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142000/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "56d8cf97-4f74-56a0-aa68-2555b3185d47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142000/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "e7ed59c4-7f8d-511d-b2cd-912a8ca1bbd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142000/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "e36a7df3-4b60-51eb-8410-ea9f59627a4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142000/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "9a6c8134-625e-517b-b13e-9abb15edb487" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142000/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "35f9ac41-4f96-571a-8018-1cc0d2bb0983" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-142000/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-142000/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-142000/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-142000/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-142000/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-142000/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142000" :question/id #uuid "949bd398-6573-53d2-bf2d-21cf0dde3f19" :question/math-academy-id "q-142000" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069862/assets/98edb404419e7ab515109f87addb44709513007b1a0105b648a3ce2b62ad547f.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}=3.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $1$ unit up. Hence, $D=1.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=3+1=4.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)+1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-142000/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dac9c72b-c23f-56fa-b939-6e3b56d3a13b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142000"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143668/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "1ca5e747-b893-52e8-a886-2ad43b181501" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143668/selection/3ee1b31380b76296d8afa406dadf54cf58733c9ea566eeb931e4a0960a497c5a" :answer/id #uuid "0cb3db5c-e6b9-59ca-a168-2117861b71e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143668/selection/ab22b83e290700d204faf1095cfc25a4b648955dede5993efb51bc6a54cd3128" :answer/id #uuid "e29bd491-edc3-5252-a7e1-b44d9ab15add" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143668/selection/19d5466e84349f416e7f242f3eae0e8ce9f2558634cf0796beb62f8e60f5ea80" :answer/id #uuid "b94c36f6-5a86-5bea-a203-cacfb66da3ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143668/selection/75be7144d0f06979df25a4d833026b673a3f8e67075b82357bb7a90b42abaa01" :answer/id #uuid "eb51bc2d-ca9a-54b1-beaa-611941e8a47c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143668/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6d8be10-97c4-58fe-8896-2f77d8ac46b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143668/selection/3ee1b31380b76296d8afa406dadf54cf58733c9ea566eeb931e4a0960a497c5a" :answer-field/choices ["q-143668/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-143668/selection/3ee1b31380b76296d8afa406dadf54cf58733c9ea566eeb931e4a0960a497c5a" "q-143668/selection/ab22b83e290700d204faf1095cfc25a4b648955dede5993efb51bc6a54cd3128" "q-143668/selection/19d5466e84349f416e7f242f3eae0e8ce9f2558634cf0796beb62f8e60f5ea80" "q-143668/selection/75be7144d0f06979df25a4d833026b673a3f8e67075b82357bb7a90b42abaa01"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143668" :question/id #uuid "e775babe-aff7-50d7-903d-d93ed0c9bdc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-143668" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069862/assets/f6ee30d5c189c9579a1f38d59f06581a7cfff944d42489eab2e3c0c6ce089ad4.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{5\\pi }{3})}=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $\\frac{12}{5}$ units down. Hence, $D=-\\frac{12}{5}.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{3}{5}+(-\\frac{12}{5})=-\\frac{9}{5}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{3x}{5})-\\frac{12}{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143668/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dac9c72b-c23f-56fa-b939-6e3b56d3a13b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143668"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143674/selection/75d4bf82dfc61c34c77bbbf7bd5b3bd55806108bbef22fc9bcd32571f4f3b0b8" :answer/id #uuid "ccdc2494-06db-5e3c-8680-e17dc3e997e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143674/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "9e46b978-291c-5371-8332-f8ac43b31238" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143674/selection/a3f72a33bd97dbcb26e67e320a072cf6fd98f5dc94f2de44db2fa04c176254bd" :answer/id #uuid "39daa270-eb68-5ba9-84a4-cd6aee1b7ef2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143674/selection/09e535b811e1e7584404784c7ac4f577a3ed9805710046fc8fb895ffb3de13a0" :answer/id #uuid "1f00686a-47d8-510d-9126-f8a1842eb2bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143674/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" :answer/id #uuid "4e0afeb4-d0c8-524d-ab14-f1b98191d12e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143674/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4476e94-74ca-573c-b4d8-ca005305943b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143674/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-143674/selection/75d4bf82dfc61c34c77bbbf7bd5b3bd55806108bbef22fc9bcd32571f4f3b0b8" "q-143674/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-143674/selection/a3f72a33bd97dbcb26e67e320a072cf6fd98f5dc94f2de44db2fa04c176254bd" "q-143674/selection/09e535b811e1e7584404784c7ac4f577a3ed9805710046fc8fb895ffb3de13a0" "q-143674/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143674" :question/id #uuid "fb50bb2b-5c10-590e-b034-9707381ca9b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-143674" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069862/assets/ee4ad78545160a052a28f0f0fcc7df476cc2063e48429a315a9cb9242f7d5311.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x+C),$ where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of $C?$" :question/worked-solution "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x+C) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3(x+\\frac{C}{3}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $x+\\frac{C}{3}$ indicates that the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3(x+\\frac{C}{3}))$ is a horizontal translation of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x).$ Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069862/assets/e1ed3a322c82b5c70acb01c54c97b09814f41aec80d980034a6fcdc46037209c.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)$ by $\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{12}=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ units to the left. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\frac{C}{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143674/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84355770-5926-5be6-9b9f-c13bb05599ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143674"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
